  "sections": [
    {
      "section_id": "bone_saw_section_1",
      "section_title": "Bone saw",
      "section_order": 1,
      "subsections": [
        {
          "subsection_id": "bone_saw_subsection_1",
          "subsection_title": "1. Introduction",
          "subsection_icon": null,
          "content_groups": [
            {
              "group_id": "bone_saw_group_1",
              "group_title": "",
              "group_subtitle": null,
              "group_icon": null,
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "A bone saw is an orthopaedic surgical instrument designed to cut bone during surgical procedures. Depending on the design, it may be operated manually or powered by an electric or pneumatic system."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Bone saws are used in procedures such as amputations, osteotomies, joint replacement and selected reconstructive operations."
                },
                {
                  "type": "image",
                  "assetPath": "assets/resources/content/surgical/bone_saw_01.webp",
                  "caption": null
                },
                {
                  "type": "image",
                  "assetPath": "assets/resources/content/surgical/bone_saw_02.webp",
                  "caption": null
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "OSCE identification statement:"
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "“This is a bone saw, an orthopaedic surgical instrument used to divide bone during procedures such as osteotomy, amputation and joint replacement. Bone saws may be manual or powered, with different blade designs selected according to the bone, procedure and required precision.”",
                  "style": "quote"
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "subsection_id": "bone_saw_subsection_2",
          "subsection_title": "2. Classification of bone saws",
          "subsection_icon": null,
          "content_groups": [
            {
              "group_id": "bone_saw_group_2",
              "group_title": "A. According to power source",
              "group_subtitle": null,
              "group_icon": null,
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "type": "image",
                  "assetPath": "assets/resources/content/surgical/bone_saw_03.webp",
                  "caption": null
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "1. Manual bone saw"
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Operated by the surgeon using hand movements."
                },
                {
                  "type": "list",
                  "items": [
                    {
                      "text": "Does not require a motor or power supply.",
                      "level": 0
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "Includes traditional amputation and orthopaedic saw designs.",
                      "level": 0
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "Cutting speed depends on the operator and the saw design.",
                      "level": 0
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "image",
                  "assetPath": "assets/resources/content/surgical/bone_saw_01.webp",
                  "caption": null
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "2. Powered bone saw"
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Uses an electric or pneumatic handpiece to drive the blade."
                },
                {
                  "type": "list",
                  "items": [
                    {
                      "text": "Common in modern orthopaedic surgery.",
                      "level": 0
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "Provides rapid, controlled cutting when correctly operated.",
                      "level": 0
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "Requires appropriate power equipment, compatible blades and maintenance.",
                      "level": 0
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "group_id": "bone_saw_group_3",
              "group_title": "B. According to blade movement or design",
              "group_subtitle": null,
              "group_icon": null,
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "type": "image",
                  "assetPath": "assets/resources/content/surgical/bone_saw_04.webp",
                  "caption": null
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "1. Oscillating saw"
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "The blade moves rapidly back and forth through a limited angle. Widely used for controlled bone cuts in joint replacement and other orthopaedic procedures."
                },
                {
                  "type": "image",
                  "assetPath": "assets/resources/content/surgical/bone_saw_05.webp",
                  "caption": null
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "2. Reciprocating saw"
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "The blade moves repeatedly in a linear direction. Used for selected orthopaedic cuts according to the device and procedure."
                },
                {
                  "type": "image",
                  "assetPath": "assets/resources/content/surgical/bone_saw_06.webp",
                  "caption": null
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "3. Wire saw"
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "A flexible cutting wire with a serrated surface, such as a Gigli saw. It can pass around bone where access for a rigid blade is limited."
                },
                {
                  "type": "image",
                  "assetPath": "assets/resources/content/surgical/bone_saw_07.webp",
                  "caption": null
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "4. Traditional rigid bone saw"
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "A hand-operated saw with a rigid serrated blade, used in selected bone-cutting procedures."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Important distinction: A Gigli saw is a specific type of flexible wire saw. It is not the same as a powered oscillating or reciprocating saw."
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "subsection_id": "bone_saw_subsection_3",
          "subsection_title": "3. Labelled components",
          "subsection_icon": null,
          "content_groups": [
            {
              "group_id": "bone_saw_group_4",
              "group_title": "",
              "group_subtitle": null,
              "group_icon": null,
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "The components depend on the type of bone saw. In an OSCE, identify the parts present on the instrument in front of you rather than assuming every saw has the same structure."
                },
                {
                  "type": "image",
                  "assetPath": "assets/resources/content/surgical/bone_saw_08.webp",
                  "caption": null
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "ebay.com"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "group_id": "bone_saw_group_5",
              "group_title": "A. Powered bone saw",
              "group_subtitle": null,
              "group_icon": null,
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "1. Handpiece or handle"
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "The portion held by the surgeon; provides control and houses or connects to the drive mechanism."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "2. Cutting blade"
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "The toothed metal component that cuts bone. Blade shape and tooth pattern depend on the intended procedure."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "3. Blade attachment or locking mechanism"
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Secures the blade to the handpiece and prevents unintended detachment."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "4. Drive mechanism"
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Produces the oscillating or reciprocating motion, depending on the saw design."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "5. Power connection or battery"
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Supplies energy to the handpiece. This may be a cable, battery or pneumatic connection, depending on the system."
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "group_id": "bone_saw_group_6",
              "group_title": "B. Manual bone saw",
              "group_subtitle": null,
              "group_icon": null,
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "type": "list",
                  "title": "The main components are:",
                  "items": [
                    {
                      "text": "Handle: provides grip and control.",
                      "level": 0
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "Blade: rigid metal cutting component.",
                      "level": 0
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "Teeth: serrated cutting edge that removes bone during movement.",
                      "level": 0
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "Blade frame or tensioning mechanism: present on certain designs, but not all manual bone saws.",
                      "level": 0
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "subsection_id": "bone_saw_subsection_4",
          "subsection_title": "4. Properties of a bone saw",
          "subsection_icon": null,
          "content_groups": [
            {
              "group_id": "bone_saw_group_7",
              "group_title": "",
              "group_subtitle": null,
              "group_icon": null,
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "type": "list",
                  "title": "A bone saw generally has the following characteristics:",
                  "items": [
                    {
                      "text": "A strong cutting blade suitable for mineralised bone.",
                      "level": 0
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "Teeth designed to cut through bone efficiently.",
                      "level": 0
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "A handle or handpiece that allows controlled manipulation.",
                      "level": 0
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "A blade configuration suited to the anatomical site and intended cut.",
                      "level": 0
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "For powered saws, a drive system that produces the specified blade movement.",
                      "level": 0
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "Compatibility with the appropriate sterilisation or reprocessing protocol, where reusable.",
                      "level": 0
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "The blade must be compatible with the specific handpiece. Not every blade fits every powered saw."
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "subsection_id": "bone_saw_subsection_5",
          "subsection_title": "5. Principles of operation",
          "subsection_icon": null,
          "content_groups": [
            {
              "group_id": "bone_saw_group_8",
              "group_title": "",
              "group_subtitle": null,
              "group_icon": null,
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "A bone saw cuts bone by applying repeated mechanical force through a toothed blade."
                },
                {
                  "type": "list",
                  "items": [
                    {
                      "text": "A manual saw relies on the operator's movement.",
                      "level": 0
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "An oscillating saw uses rapid angular movement.",
                      "level": 0
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "A reciprocating saw uses repeated linear movement.",
                      "level": 0
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "A wire saw cuts through repeated movement of a serrated flexible wire.",
                      "level": 0
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "The objective is to achieve the required bone division while limiting unintended injury to surrounding tissues and avoiding excessive heat generation."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "In powered bone surgery, irrigation and appropriate technique may be needed to reduce thermal injury, depending on the procedure and device."
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "subsection_id": "bone_saw_subsection_6",
          "subsection_title": "6. Indications and clinical uses",
          "subsection_icon": null,
          "content_groups": [
            {
              "group_id": "bone_saw_group_9",
              "group_title": "",
              "group_subtitle": null,
              "group_icon": null,
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "type": "image",
                  "assetPath": "assets/resources/content/surgical/bone_saw_09.webp",
                  "caption": null
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "1. Joint replacement surgery"
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Powered oscillating saws are used to make planned bone cuts during procedures such as total knee arthroplasty."
                },
                {
                  "type": "image",
                  "assetPath": "assets/resources/content/surgical/bone_saw_10.webp",
                  "caption": null
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "2. Osteotomy"
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Bone is deliberately divided to correct deformity, alter alignment or change joint mechanics."
                },
                {
                  "type": "image",
                  "assetPath": "assets/resources/content/surgical/bone_saw_02.webp",
                  "caption": null
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "3. Amputation"
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "A bone saw may be used to divide the bone during selected limb amputations."
                },
                {
                  "type": "image",
                  "assetPath": "assets/resources/content/surgical/bone_saw_11.webp",
                  "caption": null
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "4. Bone reconstruction and revision procedures"
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Used in selected reconstructive procedures that require controlled removal or reshaping of bone."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Other uses include selected corrective foot operations, craniofacial procedures, and removal or reshaping of bone during specific orthopaedic operations."
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "subsection_id": "bone_saw_subsection_7",
          "subsection_title": "7. Advantages",
          "subsection_icon": null,
          "content_groups": [
            {
              "group_id": "bone_saw_group_10",
              "group_title": "",
              "group_subtitle": null,
              "group_icon": null,
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "type": "list",
                  "items": [
                    {
                      "text": "Allows controlled division of bone.",
                      "level": 0
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "Powered designs can cut bone rapidly.",
                      "level": 0
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "Different blade shapes accommodate different anatomical requirements.",
                      "level": 0
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "Can produce accurate, planned bone cuts when used correctly.",
                      "level": 0
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "Wire saws can reach bone that is difficult to access with a rigid blade.",
                      "level": 0
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "Manual saws do not require a powered drive system.",
                      "level": 0
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "subsection_id": "bone_saw_subsection_8",
          "subsection_title": "8. Disadvantages",
          "subsection_icon": null,
          "content_groups": [
            {
              "group_id": "bone_saw_group_11",
              "group_title": "",
              "group_subtitle": null,
              "group_icon": null,
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "type": "list",
                  "items": [
                    {
                      "text": "Can injure adjacent soft tissues, vessels or nerves.",
                      "level": 0
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "Powered saws require compatible equipment and maintenance.",
                      "level": 0
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "Excessive pressure or poor technique may produce heat and bone damage.",
                      "level": 0
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "Blades can become blunt, damaged or contaminated.",
                      "level": 0
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "Powered devices may generate noise and vibration.",
                      "level": 0
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "Wire saws can be difficult to control if improperly positioned or tensioned.",
                      "level": 0
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "A rigid saw may be unsuitable where access is restricted.",
                      "level": 0
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "subsection_id": "bone_saw_subsection_9",
          "subsection_title": "9. Contraindications and precautions",
          "subsection_icon": null,
          "content_groups": [
            {
              "group_id": "bone_saw_group_12",
              "group_title": "",
              "group_subtitle": null,
              "group_icon": null,
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "There is no universal contraindication to bone saw use; suitability depends on the planned procedure and the patient's condition."
                },
                {
                  "type": "list",
                  "title": "Important precautions include:",
                  "items": [
                    {
                      "text": "Confirming the correct instrument and blade for the procedure.",
                      "level": 0
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "Protecting nearby nerves, vessels, tendons and soft tissues.",
                      "level": 0
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "Ensuring the bone is exposed and the cut is appropriately planned.",
                      "level": 0
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "Checking that the blade is secure and the equipment is functioning correctly.",
                      "level": 0
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "Using irrigation or other heat-control measures when indicated.",
                      "level": 0
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "Avoiding excessive pressure and uncontrolled movement.",
                      "level": 0
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "Following appropriate precautions for powered equipment, sterile fields and instrument reprocessing.",
                      "level": 0
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "A bone saw is not used merely because a fracture is present. Its use must be justified by the required surgical procedure."
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "subsection_id": "bone_saw_subsection_10",
          "subsection_title": "10. Basic principles of safe use",
          "subsection_icon": null,
          "content_groups": [
            {
              "group_id": "bone_saw_group_13",
              "group_title": "",
              "group_subtitle": null,
              "group_icon": null,
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "For OSCE understanding; actual bone cutting requires surgical training and appropriate supervision."
                },
                {
                  "type": "list",
                  "items": [
                    {
                      "text": "Confirm the indication and planned bone cut.",
                      "level": 0,
                      "label": "1."
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "Check the instrument, blade and compatibility of the components.",
                      "level": 0,
                      "label": "2."
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "Ensure the surgical field and surrounding tissues are appropriately protected.",
                      "level": 0,
                      "label": "3."
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "Position and expose the bone according to the procedure.",
                      "level": 0,
                      "label": "4."
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "Use the saw with controlled movements and the correct technique for the device.",
                      "level": 0,
                      "label": "5."
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "Apply irrigation or heat-control measures when indicated.",
                      "level": 0,
                      "label": "6."
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "Avoid unintended injury to adjacent anatomical structures.",
                      "level": 0,
                      "label": "7."
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "Inspect the cut and manage bone edges according to the procedure.",
                      "level": 0,
                      "label": "8."
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "Check the instrument and blade for damage after use.",
                      "level": 0,
                      "label": "9."
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "subsection_id": "bone_saw_subsection_11",
          "subsection_title": "11. Complications",
          "subsection_icon": null,
          "content_groups": [
            {
              "group_id": "bone_saw_group_14",
              "group_title": "",
              "group_subtitle": null,
              "group_icon": null,
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "type": "table",
                  "columns": [
                    "Complication",
                    "Explanation"
                  ],
                  "rows": [
                    [
                      "Soft-tissue injury",
                      "Accidental damage to skin, muscle, tendon or other tissue."
                    ],
                    [
                      "Neurovascular injury",
                      "Damage to nearby nerves or blood vessels."
                    ],
                    [
                      "Thermal necrosis",
                      "Heat generated during cutting damages bone tissue."
                    ],
                    [
                      "Incomplete or inaccurate cut",
                      "May compromise the intended surgical result."
                    ],
                    [
                      "Excessive bone loss",
                      "An imprecise cut can remove more bone than intended."
                    ],
                    [
                      "Blade breakage",
                      "A damaged or unsuitable blade may fracture."
                    ],
                    [
                      "Infection",
                      "Can occur if appropriate aseptic practices are not maintained."
                    ],
                    [
                      "Bone splintering or cracking",
                      "May occur depending on bone quality, technique and the procedure."
                    ],
                    [
                      "Injury to adjacent structures",
                      "Particularly important when cutting near joints or vulnerable anatomical structures."
                    ]
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "subsection_id": "bone_saw_subsection_12",
          "subsection_title": "12. Common OSCE viva questions",
          "subsection_icon": null,
          "content_groups": [
            {
              "group_id": "bone_saw_group_15",
              "group_title": "",
              "group_subtitle": null,
              "group_icon": null,
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Q1. What is a bone saw?"
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "An orthopaedic surgical instrument used to divide bone during procedures such as osteotomy, amputation and joint replacement."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Q2. Name four types of bone saw."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Manual rigid bone saw, powered oscillating saw, powered reciprocating saw and wire saw."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Q3. What is an oscillating saw used for?"
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "It makes controlled bone cuts in selected orthopaedic procedures, including joint replacement."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Q4. What is a Gigli saw?"
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "A flexible wire saw with a serrated cutting surface, operated by moving the wire back and forth around bone."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Q5. Name three complications of bone saw use."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Thermal bone injury, soft-tissue injury and neurovascular injury."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Q6. Why may irrigation be required?"
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "To help dissipate heat and reduce the risk of thermal injury during cutting, when indicated by the procedure."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Q7. What must be checked before using a powered bone saw?"
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "The blade's condition and compatibility, secure attachment, proper equipment function and readiness of the operative setup."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Q8. Differentiate a bone saw from an osteotome."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "A bone saw divides bone using a toothed blade. An osteotome is a chisel-like instrument used to cut or shape bone, often with controlled blows from a mallet or by hand, depending on the technique."
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
